{"sounds":[{"ipa":"iː","kind":"vowel","tip":"Long and tense, like a long Turkish \"i\". Smile slightly.","tipTr":"Uzun ve gergin \"i\". Hafifçe gülümser gibi. sheep /ʃiːp/ ≠ ship /ʃɪp/.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"see","us":"siː","uk":"siː"},{"w":"eat","us":"iːt","uk":"iːt"},{"w":"green","us":"ɡriːn","uk":"ɡriːn"}]},{"ipa":"ɪ","kind":"vowel","tip":"Short and relaxed, between Turkish \"i\" and \"e\".","tipTr":"Kısa ve gevşek; Türkçe \"i\" ile \"e\" arası. Türkçe \"i\" gibi söylerseniz ship, sheep'e benzer.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"sit","us":"sɪt","uk":"sɪt"},{"w":"big","us":"bɪɡ","uk":"bɪɡ"},{"w":"fish","us":"fɪʃ","uk":"fɪʃ"}]},{"ipa":"e","kind":"vowel","tip":"Like Turkish \"e\" in \"ev\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"ev\" kelimesindeki e.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"bed","us":"bɛd","uk":"bed"},{"w":"red","us":"rɛd","uk":"red"},{"w":"said","us":"sɛd","uk":"sed"}]},{"ipa":"æ","kind":"vowel","tip":"Open your mouth wide, between \"a\" and \"e\".","tipTr":"Ağzı geniş açarak \"a\" ile \"e\" arası bir ses. Türkçede yok: bad /bæd/ ≠ bed /bed/.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"cat","us":"kæt","uk":"kæt"},{"w":"bad","us":"bæd","uk":"bæd"},{"w":"apple","us":"ˈæpəl","uk":"ˈæpəl"}]},{"ipa":"ʌ","kind":"vowel","tip":"A short central \"a\".","tipTr":"Kısa, ağzın ortasında bir \"a\". cup /kʌp/ ≠ cap /kæp/.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"cup","us":"kʌp","uk":"kʌp"},{"w":"love","us":"lʌv","uk":"lʌv"},{"w":"money","us":"ˈmʌni","uk":"ˈmʌni"}]},{"ipa":"ɑː","kind":"vowel","tip":"A long open \"a\" from the back of the mouth.","tipTr":"Uzun ve açık, boğaza yakın bir \"a\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"car","us":"kɑːr","uk":"kɑː"},{"w":"father","us":"ˈfɑːðɚ","uk":"ˈfɑːðə"},{"w":"start","us":"stɑːrt","uk":"stɑːt"}]},{"ipa":"ɒ","kind":"vowel","tip":"Short rounded \"o\" (British).","tipTr":"Kısa, yuvarlak \"o\" (İngiliz İngilizcesi). Amerikan aksanında genelde /ɑː/ olur.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"hot","us":"hɑːt","uk":"hɒt"},{"w":"dog","us":"dɔːɡ","uk":"dɒɡ"},{"w":"stop","us":"stɑːp","uk":"stɒp"}]},{"ipa":"ɔː","kind":"vowel","tip":"Long rounded \"o\".","tipTr":"Uzun ve yuvarlak \"o\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"four","us":"fɔːr","uk":"fɔː"},{"w":"law","us":"lɔː","uk":"lɔː"},{"w":"walk","us":"wɔːk","uk":"wɔːk"}]},{"ipa":"ʊ","kind":"vowel","tip":"Short relaxed \"u\".","tipTr":"Kısa ve gevşek \"u\". full /fʊl/ ≠ fool /fuːl/.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"book","us":"bʊk","uk":"bʊk"},{"w":"put","us":"pʊt","uk":"pʊt"},{"w":"good","us":"ɡʊd","uk":"ɡʊd"}]},{"ipa":"uː","kind":"vowel","tip":"Long \"u\" with rounded lips.","tipTr":"Dudaklar yuvarlak, uzun \"u\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"food","us":"fuːd","uk":"fuːd"},{"w":"blue","us":"bluː","uk":"bluː"},{"w":"you","us":"juː","uk":"jə"}]},{"ipa":"ɜː","kind":"vowel","tip":"A long central sound, close to Turkish \"ö\" with relaxed lips.","tipTr":"Türkçe \"ö\" sesine yakın ama dudaklar yuvarlanmaz. work /wɜːk/ ≠ walk /wɔːk/.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"bird","us":"bɝːd","uk":"bɜːd"},{"w":"work","us":"wɝːk","uk":"wɜːk"},{"w":"learn","us":"lɝːn","uk":"lɜːn"}]},{"ipa":"ə","kind":"vowel","tip":"Schwa: the most common English vowel. Short, weak, unstressed.","tipTr":"Schwa: İngilizcenin en sık ünlüsü. Kısa, zayıf, vurgusuz bir \"ı\" gibi. Türkçe konuşanlar her harfi tam okuma eğiliminde; vurgusuz heceleri zayıflatmak doğal aksanın anahtarıdır.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"about","us":"əˈbaʊt","uk":"əˈbaʊt"},{"w":"banana","us":"bəˈnænə","uk":"bəˈnɑːnə"},{"w":"teacher","us":"ˈtiːtʃɚ","uk":"ˈtiːtʃə"}]},{"ipa":"eɪ","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from \"e\" to \"i\".","tipTr":"\"e\"den \"i\"ye kayan ses: \"ey\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"day","us":"deɪ","uk":"deɪ"},{"w":"name","us":"neɪm","uk":"neɪm"},{"w":"rain","us":"reɪn","uk":"reɪn"}]},{"ipa":"aɪ","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from \"a\" to \"i\".","tipTr":"\"ay\" gibi.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"my","us":"maɪ","uk":"maɪ"},{"w":"time","us":"taɪm","uk":"taɪm"},{"w":"buy","us":"baɪ","uk":"baɪ"}]},{"ipa":"ɔɪ","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from \"o\" to \"i\".","tipTr":"\"oy\" gibi.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"boy","us":"bɔɪ","uk":"bɔɪ"},{"w":"coin","us":"kɔɪn","uk":"kɔɪn"},{"w":"enjoy","us":"ˌɛnˈdʒɔɪ","uk":"enˈdʒɔɪ"}]},{"ipa":"aʊ","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from \"a\" to \"u\".","tipTr":"\"av\" ile \"au\" arası.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"now","us":"naʊ","uk":"naʊ"},{"w":"house","us":"haʊs","uk":"haʊs"},{"w":"out","us":"aʊt","uk":"aʊt"}]},{"ipa":"əʊ","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from schwa to \"u\" (British). American: oʊ.","tipTr":"İngiliz: \"ıu\", Amerikan: \"ou\". Düz bir \"o\" söylemeyin: go ≠ \"go\".","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"go","us":"ɡoʊ","uk":"ɡəʊ"},{"w":"home","us":"hoʊm","uk":"həʊm"},{"w":"know","us":"noʊ","uk":"nəʊ"}]},{"ipa":"ɪə","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from \"ɪ\" to schwa (British).","tipTr":"\"iı\" gibi (İngiliz).","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"near","us":"nɪr","uk":"nɪə"},{"w":"here","us":"hiːr","uk":"hɪə"},{"w":"idea","us":"aɪˈdiːə","uk":"aɪˈdɪə"}]},{"ipa":"eə","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from \"e\" to schwa (British).","tipTr":"\"eı\" gibi (İngiliz).","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"hair","us":"hɛr","uk":"heə"},{"w":"care","us":"kɛr","uk":"keə"},{"w":"where","us":"wɛr","uk":"weə"}]},{"ipa":"ʊə","kind":"diphthong","tip":"Glide from \"ʊ\" to schwa (often /ɔː/ today).","tipTr":"\"uı\" gibi; bugün çoğu zaman /ɔː/ söylenir.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"tour","us":"tʊr","uk":"tʊə"},{"w":"pure","us":"pjʊr","uk":"pjʊə"},{"w":"cure","us":"kjʊr","uk":"kjʊə"}]},{"ipa":"p","kind":"consonant","tip":"With a puff of air at the start of a stressed syllable.","tipTr":"Vurgulu hece başında hafif bir hava püskürmesiyle.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"pen","us":"pɛn","uk":"pen"},{"w":"happy","us":"ˈhæpi","uk":"ˈhæpi"},{"w":"stop","us":"stɑːp","uk":"stɒp"}]},{"ipa":"b","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"b\". Keep it voiced at the end of words.","tipTr":"Türkçe \"b\". Kelime sonunda \"p\"ye çevirmeyin: job ≠ \"jop\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"bad","us":"bæd","uk":"bæd"},{"w":"baby","us":"ˈbeɪbi","uk":"ˈbeɪbi"},{"w":"job","us":"dʒɑːb","uk":"dʒɒb"}]},{"ipa":"t","kind":"consonant","tip":"Tongue behind the top teeth. In American English, between vowels it can sound like a quick \"d\".","tipTr":"Dil üst dişlerin arkasında. Amerikan aksanında iki ünlü arasında hızlı bir \"d\" gibi: water \"wadır\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"ten","us":"tɛn","uk":"ten"},{"w":"water","us":"ˈwɔːtɚ","uk":"ˈwɔːtə"},{"w":"cat","us":"kæt","uk":"kæt"}]},{"ipa":"d","kind":"consonant","tip":"Voiced; don't turn it into \"t\" at the end.","tipTr":"Kelime sonunda \"t\"ye çevirmeyin: bed ≠ bet.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"dog","us":"dɔːɡ","uk":"dɒɡ"},{"w":"ladder","us":"ˈlædɚ","uk":"ˈlædə"},{"w":"bed","us":"bɛd","uk":"bed"}]},{"ipa":"k","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"k\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"k\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"cat","us":"kæt","uk":"kæt"},{"w":"school","us":"skuːl","uk":"skuːl"},{"w":"back","us":"bæk","uk":"bæk"}]},{"ipa":"ɡ","kind":"consonant","tip":"Voiced; keep it at the end of words.","tipTr":"Sonda \"k\"ye çevirmeyin: dog ≠ dock.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"go","us":"ɡoʊ","uk":"ɡəʊ"},{"w":"bigger","us":"ˈbɪɡɚ","uk":"ˈbɪɡə"},{"w":"dog","us":"dɔːɡ","uk":"dɒɡ"}]},{"ipa":"f","kind":"consonant","tip":"Top teeth on the bottom lip.","tipTr":"Üst dişler alt dudağa değer.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"fish","us":"fɪʃ","uk":"fɪʃ"},{"w":"coffee","us":"ˈkɑːfi","uk":"ˈkɒfi"},{"w":"laugh","us":"læf","uk":"lɑːf"}]},{"ipa":"v","kind":"consonant","tip":"Top teeth touch the bottom lip and the sound vibrates. Not \"w\".","tipTr":"Üst dişler alt dudağa değer ve titreşir. \"w\" ile karıştırmayın: very ≠ \"wery\", vine ≠ wine.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"very","us":"ˈvɛri","uk":"ˈveri"},{"w":"river","us":"ˈrɪvɚ","uk":"ˈrɪvə"},{"w":"love","us":"lʌv","uk":"lʌv"}]},{"ipa":"θ","kind":"consonant","tip":"Tongue tip between the teeth, blow air. No voice.","tipTr":"Dil ucu dişlerin arasında, sessizce hava üfleyin. \"t\" ya da \"s\" değil: think ≠ \"tink\"/\"sink\".","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"think","us":"θɪŋk","uk":"θɪŋk"},{"w":"three","us":"θriː","uk":"θriː"},{"w":"bath","us":"bæθ","uk":"bɑːθ"}]},{"ipa":"ð","kind":"consonant","tip":"Tongue between the teeth, with voice.","tipTr":"Dil dişlerin arasında, titreşimli. \"d\" ya da \"z\" değil: they ≠ \"dey\".","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"this","us":"ðɪs","uk":"ðɪs"},{"w":"mother","us":"ˈmʌðɚ","uk":"ˈmʌðə"},{"w":"with","us":"wɪð","uk":"wɪð"}]},{"ipa":"s","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"s\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"s\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"see","us":"siː","uk":"siː"},{"w":"class","us":"klæs","uk":"klɑːs"},{"w":"city","us":"ˈsɪti","uk":"ˈsɪti"}]},{"ipa":"z","kind":"consonant","tip":"Voiced \"s\". Plural -s is often /z/: dogs /dɒɡz/.","tipTr":"Titreşimli s. Çoğul -s çoğu zaman /z/ okunur: dogs \"dogz\", is \"iz\".","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"zoo","us":"zuː","uk":"zuː"},{"w":"easy","us":"ˈiːzi","uk":"ˈiːzi"},{"w":"is","us":"ɪz","uk":"ɪz"}]},{"ipa":"ʃ","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"ş\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"ş\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"she","us":"ʃiː","uk":"ʃiː"},{"w":"sugar","us":"ˈʃʊɡɚ","uk":"ˈʃʊɡə"},{"w":"fish","us":"fɪʃ","uk":"fɪʃ"}]},{"ipa":"ʒ","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"j\" in \"jale\".","tipTr":"\"Jale\"deki j.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"vision","us":"ˈvɪʒən","uk":"ˈvɪʒən"},{"w":"measure","us":"ˈmɛʒɚ","uk":"ˈmeʒə"},{"w":"usually","us":"ˈjuːʒəwəli","uk":"ˈjuːʒʊəli"}]},{"ipa":"h","kind":"consonant","tip":"A soft breath, lighter than Turkish \"h\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"h\"den daha hafif, sadece nefes.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"hat","us":"hæt","uk":"hæt"},{"w":"behind","us":"bɪˈhaɪnd","uk":"bɪˈhaɪnd"},{"w":"who","us":"huː","uk":"huː"}]},{"ipa":"tʃ","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"ç\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"ç\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"chair","us":"tʃɛr","uk":"tʃeə"},{"w":"teacher","us":"ˈtiːtʃɚ","uk":"ˈtiːtʃə"},{"w":"watch","us":"wɑːtʃ","uk":"wɒtʃ"}]},{"ipa":"dʒ","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"c\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"c\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"job","us":"dʒɑːb","uk":"dʒɒb"},{"w":"age","us":"eɪdʒ","uk":"eɪdʒ"},{"w":"bridge","us":"brɪdʒ","uk":"brɪdʒ"}]},{"ipa":"m","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"m\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"m\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"man","us":"mæn","uk":"mæn"},{"w":"summer","us":"ˈsʌmɚ","uk":"ˈsʌmə"},{"w":"time","us":"taɪm","uk":"taɪm"}]},{"ipa":"n","kind":"consonant","tip":"Like Turkish \"n\".","tipTr":"Türkçe \"n\".","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"no","us":"noʊ","uk":"nəʊ"},{"w":"dinner","us":"ˈdɪnɚ","uk":"ˈdɪnə"},{"w":"sun","us":"sʌn","uk":"sʌn"}]},{"ipa":"ŋ","kind":"consonant","tip":"Back of the tongue up, sound through the nose. Usually no \"g\" after it.","tipTr":"Genizden gelen \"n\"; arkasından \"g\" okunmaz: sing \"sin(g)\", \"sing-g\" değil.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"sing","us":"sɪŋ","uk":"sɪŋ"},{"w":"thinking","us":"ˈθɪŋkɪŋ","uk":"ˈθɪŋkɪŋ"},{"w":"long","us":"lɔːŋ","uk":"lɒŋ"}]},{"ipa":"l","kind":"consonant","tip":"At the end of words it is \"dark\", like the Turkish \"l\" in \"kal\".","tipTr":"Kelime sonunda kalın l, Türkçe \"kal\" kelimesindeki gibi.","hard":false,"examples":[{"w":"leg","us":"lɛɡ","uk":"leɡ"},{"w":"hello","us":"həˈloʊ","uk":"heˈləʊ"},{"w":"feel","us":"fiːl","uk":"fiːl"}]},{"ipa":"r","kind":"consonant","tip":"The tongue doesn't touch the roof of the mouth; no rolling. British English drops it after vowels (car /kɑː/).","tipTr":"Dil damağa değmez, Türkçedeki gibi titretilmez. İngiliz aksanında ünlüden sonra okunmaz (car /kɑː/), Amerikan aksanında okunur.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"red","us":"rɛd","uk":"red"},{"w":"sorry","us":"ˈsɑːri","uk":"ˈsɒri"},{"w":"car","us":"kɑːr","uk":"kɑː"}]},{"ipa":"w","kind":"consonant","tip":"Round your lips like \"u\" and move quickly. Teeth don't touch the lip.","tipTr":"Dudakları \"u\" gibi yuvarlayıp hızlıca açın; dişler dudağa değmez. wet ≠ vet.","hard":true,"examples":[{"w":"we","us":"wiː","uk":"wiː"},{"w":"away"